   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Global Fund to Fight AIDS, Tuberculosis and Malaria</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale Up Interventions to Fight against Malaria in the Union of the Comoros - Comoros (01-Apr-2012-30-Sep-2015)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaria is the leading cause of death recorded in public and private health facilities in the Union of the Comoros. The most vulnerable groups are children under age 5 and pregnant women. The overall goal of the program supported by this grant is to reduce the prevalence of malaria by at least 50 percent by 2014. Planned activities include: free distribution of insecticide-treated nets through mass campaigns and distributions in prenatal consultation centers; indoor residual spraying; the extension of intermittent preventive treatment coverage; the introduction of rapid diagnostic tests; the provision of artemisinin-based combination therapy for the treatment of malaria; and the provision of technical assistance to the national program.</narrative>
  </description>
